  abstract = {We describe our high-resolution measurements of the 133C⁢s 6⁢𝑝 2𝑃3/2 state hyperfine structure. An optically narrowed diode laser excites perpendicularly a highly collimated atomic beam. The spectra are calibrated with a stable reference diode laser using a rf locking scheme allowing us to determine the splittings with an accuracy of ≤2 k⁢H⁡z, an order of magnitude better than previous results. The magnetic dipole 𝑎, electric quadrupole 𝑏, and magnetic octupole 𝑐 hyperfine coupling constants are determined. The values we obtained are 𝑎 =50.288 27⁢(23) M⁢H⁡z, 𝑏 =−0.4934⁢(17) M⁢H⁡z, and 𝑐 =0.56⁢(7) k⁢H⁡z. This work represents the first observation of the magnetic octupole moment of the cesium nucleus. We carry out atomic-structure calculations and determine the nuclear electric quadrupole moment 𝑄 =−3.55⁢(4) m⁢b and nuclear magnetic octupole moment 𝛺 =0.82⁢(10) b ×𝜇𝑁.},
  file = {/Users/jaime/Zotero/storage/49JXV79T/Gerginov et al. - 2003 - Observation of the Nuclear Magnetic Octupole Moment of $^ 133 mathrm C mathrm s $.pdf;/Users/jaime/Zotero/storage/YSISATUQ/PhysRevLett.91.html},
